    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεο-τέρᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with divine portents</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάναι</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ</span>., of Io's wanderings, dithyrambic
			phrase in <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				91
			</span></i> codd. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεο-τερπής</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, of a dish, <i>fit for the
			gods</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philox.
				2.9
			</span></i>; <i>pleasing to God</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιοτή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.197
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Marin.
			</span></i>); cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοταρπέες</span>.</div>
